@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Prune Orphans Command
  "CLI handler for mason prune: garbage-collect unreferenced blobs."

  Provides:
    - cli.newPruneCommand @source("symbol:newPruneCommand")
    - cli.defaultPruneRun @source("symbol:defaultPruneRun")

  Consumes:
    - links.Service.Prune
    - cli.shareStack
    - output.WriteJSON
    - output.HumanSize

  Invariants:
    - defaultPruneRun MUST dry-run unless --yes is set and --dry-run is not
    - Human output MUST distinguish Would prune vs Pruned and prompt for --yes when dry-run
    - JSON output MUST use the stable pruneJSON shape under output.Success

  Scenario (happy-path): Dry-run prune
    Given orphaned blobs exist
    When mason prune runs without --yes
    Then stdout reports would-prune and does not delete

  Scenario (happy-path): Confirmed prune
    Given --yes without --dry-run
    When prune succeeds
    Then stdout reports Pruned and deleted is true in JSON

  Scenario (negative): Prune failure
    Given Prune returns an error
    When the command runs
    Then emitError renders the failure
